class:: DarkVelvetProfile
summary:: Prepared sparse-tail envelope and spectral dictionary probabilities
categories:: UGens>Reverbs, Libraries>CamaraObscura
related:: Guides/CamaraObscura, Classes/DarkVelvetReverb

description::

DarkVelvetProfile prepares the time-varying energy, pulse-density scale, and
six dictionary-filter probabilities used by link::Classes/DarkVelvetReverb::.
It is based on the extended dark velvet noise formulation of Fagerström,
Schlecht, and Välimäki (2024), with an original fixed buffer format and
deterministic generator.

The profile stores piecewise-linear dB endpoints. It does not store audio and
does not perform convolution. The closest vanilla facility is an envelope
stored in a Buffer; this model additionally carries spectral probabilities,
duration, version, sample rate, seed, and validation metadata.

classmethods::

method:: exponential
Create a two-point exponential-amplitude tail.

argument:: duration
Tail duration in seconds, greater than zero and at most 30.

argument:: t60
Amplitude T60 in seconds.

argument:: bands
Reserved compatibility argument. The current dictionary has six filters.

argument:: sampleRate
Exact server sample rate expected by the renderer.

argument:: seed
Deterministic model seed.

method:: envelope
Create an arbitrary piecewise dB profile.

argument:: times
Increasing seconds beginning at zero and ending at or before 30 seconds.

argument:: levels
dB values corresponding one-to-one with code::times::.

argument:: filters
Nil for the default darkening evolution, six weights shared by every segment,
or one six-weight row per segment. Rows are normalized.

argument:: sampleRate
Exact renderer sample rate.

argument:: seed
Deterministic model seed.

method:: fromIR
Analyze the file associated with a Buffer, beginning at code::startTime::.

method:: fromFile
Analyze short-window late RMS from an audio file. This prepares a broadband
profile; it is not a full bandwise RIR fitter.

method:: read
Read a version-1 CamaraObscura text model.

instancemethods::

method:: validate
Validate metadata, segment continuity, duration, density, and filter
probabilities.

method:: summary
Return model family, version, payload size, sample rate, channels, and seed.

method:: load
Upload the serialized model to a mono server Buffer.

method:: write
Write the portable line-oriented prepared-model format.

method:: free
Free the last Buffer returned by code::load::.

method:: plotEnvelope
Plot prepared broadband dB endpoints.

method:: plotBandEnergy
Plot the six dictionary probabilities by segment.

examples::

code::
(
var profile = DarkVelvetProfile.exponential(
    4, 2.5, sampleRate: 48000, seed: 17
);
profile.summary.postln;
profile.plotEnvelope;
)
::

code::
(
var profile = DarkVelvetProfile.envelope(
    [0, 0.6, 1.8, 3],
    [-60, 0, -15, -80],
    [
        [1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0],
        [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1],
        [4, 0, 1, 3, 0, 0]
    ],
    sampleRate: 48000,
    seed: 3
);
profile.validate;
profile.plotBandEnergy;
)
::

